{
  "claim": "For non-headline series outside the 14-day gate with fewer than two changes in the last 14 days, narrowing the current log intervals by 25% while preserving q50 will reduce pinball loss.",
  "mechanism": "The hypothesis is that an isolated published-median change often reflects a single repricing or offer-composition event, after which the middle offers remain stable. The current intervals overstate subsequent median movement in this regime; the reported coverage of 0.92 for chg14 < 2 motivates testing narrower tails, although that aggregate includes gated cells.",
  "spec": {
    "when": {
      "all": [
        {"fact": "in37", "op": "==", "value": false},
        {"fact": "gate14", "op": "==", "value": false},
        {"fact": "chg14", "op": "<", "value": 2}
      ]
    },
    "do": {
      "action": "scale_width",
      "lo": 0.75,
      "hi": 0.75
    }
  },
  "falsification": "Reject if pooled skill fails to rise overall or in either selection half, fewer than 200 cells across at least five series actually change, headline skill falls, or fewer than 90% of the 2000 ISO-week block bootstrap resamples show improvement.",
  "prior_ids_used": [],
  "expects": "I expect a modest pooled-skill improvement from reducing tail loss during persistence after isolated changes, with headline forecasts unchanged. Existing zero-width forecasts remain unchanged, so the number of affected cells and consistency across selection halves are material uncertainties that the fixed test must resolve."
}
